---
description: Line limits for engine TypeScript, and a split is a move
globs: packages/engine/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Engine code

An implementation file has at most 400 lines. A test file (`*.test.ts`) has at most 500. Count every line, including comments and blank lines.

`npm run check` in `packages/engine` runs `node scripts/max-lines.mjs`. A file over its limit fails the check.

One file has one responsibility. A comment that belongs to a method moves with that method.

Keep the folder names `scene`, `map`, `areas`, and `minimap`. Each name is a different part of the game.

Do not add Prettier. Do not reformat a file in bulk. A split moves the code, so the diff is that move.

```ts
// Wrong: leave the comment behind, or rewrap the body while moving it.
// Advance one tick.
export function step(host: Host): void {
  host.tick();
}

// Right: the comment moves with the method, and the body stays as it was.
/** Advance one tick. */
export function step(host: Host): void {
  host.tick();
}
```
